summary:
  A key held down on a podcast row presses it on every repeat.

history:
  2026.44 lets Return, Enter and Space press a show row and a found-episode
  row, which until then only a pointer could. A held key repeats some 25
  times a second, and an episode row plays on one press and stops on the
  next: whether it was left playing would depend on when the key was let go.
  Only the first press of a held key acts.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ViewLogic.js

find:
      if (event.isAutoRepeat !== true && row.visible === true) row.clicked();

replace:
      if (row.visible === true) row.clicked();

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_viewrules.qml::test_a_key_held_down_presses_the_row_once
  and tests/qml/tst_rowkeys.qml::test_a_key_held_down_on_an_episode_leaves_it_playing.
  Line-neutral.
